From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:35:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(debug): capture fling tail timing and placement

Shared tracing and tests with Mihon 0080. The user identifies stutter near the end of free decay after folding, even with stable whole-fling callback rates. Preserve the first four baseline flings and the latest twelve, with bounded primitive rings for the last 64 scroll steps and actual grid draw calls. Capture unmodified requested/consumed deltas, float scroll offset, placed integer position, viewport and inclusive CPU draw wall time. Formatting occurs only at export; there is no additional frame driver, per-frame text, snapshot read or change to decay physics. Stop clears buffers and generation-safe IDs reject old flings. The added report section is separately versioned; light mode and the existing report model remain unchanged. These are diagnostics, not proof that persistent perceived jank has been fixed.
